    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d527">

                <pb facs="0969" n="929" sameAs="frus:frus1951v05/pg929"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">320/11–1551: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the United States Representative on the Palestine Conciliation
                        Commission</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Palmer</hi>), <hi rendition="#italic">at
                        Paris</hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d527-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">niact</hi>
                        
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1951-11-15T19:07:00-05:00">November 15,
                            1951—7:07 p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Gadel 158. Unpal 300. Re Palun 468, 469.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d527-f2"/>
                    In view irreconcilable positions parties as demonstrated by statements Israeli
                    and Arab Dels Dept believes conf shld be ended. Accordingly, you shld urge
                    colleagues at mtg Nov 16 advise parties conference is over, and comm shld
                    promptly set about preparation GA report.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Webb</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d527-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d527-f1-content">
                <p>Drafted by Mr. Ludlow, cleared with Mr.
                        Waldo, approved for transmission by
                    Mr. Popper, and signed for the Acting
                    Secretary by Mr. Hickerson.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d527-f2" n="2" xml:id="d527-f2-content">
                <p>Dated November 14 and 15, neither printed, these messages respectively gave the
                    Israeli and Arab Delegations’ statements on the PCC proposals (357.AC/11–1451, /11–1551).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
